# Humanities in Engineering Education.

**Authors:** Ruprecht, Robert

## Abstract
States that engineers contribute tremendously to the changing face of the earth, and the ever more urgent call for languages, management, and law competencies for engineers is an expression of the need for a grounding in humanities. Discusses the role of humanities in engineering education in the context of world economics and the role of engineers and scientists in the 20th century. (PVD)

